# Recorded verification baselines for scripts/verify.sh
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Every agent and every human composed verification ad-hoc, so every one had
# different gaps. The numbers below are the recorded truth of what a green
# tree produces. `scripts/verify.sh` compares against them rather than against
# whatever the runner happens to remember, so "it passed" means the same thing
# to everyone.
#
# The PCGen oracle pin lives separately, in scripts/pcgen-oracle-pin.env
# (sourced by verify.sh the same way as this file) — not a baseline in the
# sense below, but the same "one file, one truth" convention.
#
# HOW EACH NUMBER IS COMPARED
# ---------------------------
# Test counts are FLOORS. Adding tests never fails the gate; losing them does.
# That is the direction that matters: the failure this repo actually suffered
# was a suite silently shrinking (a fail-fast run reporting 124 of 488 suites
# as a complete pass), not a suite growing.
#
# Clippy warnings are a CEILING. New lint debt fails; paying debt down does not.
#
# WHEN THE ACTUAL EXCEEDS A FLOOR, verify.sh still passes but prints a STALE
# notice naming the new number. Updating this file is then a deliberate,
# reviewable one-line commit — never a silent drift.
#
# HOW TO RE-MEASURE
# -----------------
#   scripts/verify.sh --full --show-actuals
# prints every measured number in this file's format. Copy the ones you intend
# to move. Do not lower a floor to make a red tree green: a floor that dropped
# means tests were deleted, which is the finding, not the fix.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: THE "ENVIRONMENTAL FAILURE" FRAMING BELOW IS RETRACTED
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Eight dated revisions below assert that five suites fail "environmentally"
# on this box because it lacks fixtures under another machine's home
# directory. That assertion was WRONG for its entire recorded lifetime, and
# `ls -d /home/ubuntu` -> "No such file or directory" was repeatedly cited as
# evidence FOR the theory when it was evidence AGAINST it: the absent
# directory was not a missing environment, it was a hardcoded literal.
#
# The five suites did not need a special box. They needed a default that was
# not another user's home directory. Both operator rulings that fix this are
# recorded as durable conventions in
# `docs/release/SD-27-future-state-book-content-ingestion/decisions.md §30`:
# `$HOME`-relative paths (workspace is Syncthing-synced, so a HOME-relative
# path is correct on every machine), and build artifacts vendored into the
# build's own artifact folder rather than referenced from an external source.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-01, no PCGen environment variables set at all: the gate is
# 9 of 9, `RESULT: PASS`, exit 0, and `root-full` passes with 5930 passed
# across 533 binaries and zero `test result: FAILED` lines. The dated entries
# below stay exactly as written — they are the record of what each run
# observed, and rewriting them would falsify the audit trail this file exists
# to keep. This block is the correction; read it before believing them.
#
# COUNTING A LOG BY HAND — USE awk, NOT `grep -o` (added 2026-07-31)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The `root-full` stage FAILS on any box lacking the `/home/ubuntu/...` PCGen
# fixtures (see BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS below), and verify.sh prints a
# MEASURED block only for stages that PASSED. So that one number has always
# been re-derived by hand from the stage's log, and the notes below record the
# command each revision used:
#
# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-01 — the sentence above is no longer true, and every
# dated entry below that repeats it describes a condition that has since been
# fixed. Those entries stay as written because they are the record of what
# each run actually observed; this note is the correction, not an edit to
# them. Two changes landed together:
#   1. Every hardcoded `/home/ubuntu/...` default under `tests/`, `src/` and
#      `scripts/` became HOME-relative (`$HOME/workspace/...` in shell,
#      `std::env::var("HOME")` in Rust). `PCGEN_REPO_DIR`, `PCGEN_CORPUS_ROOT`
#      and friends still win over the default; only the fallback changed.
#      `tests/no_foreign_home_paths.rs` now fails if such a literal returns.
#   2. The two GE-05 pilot `.pcg` fixtures were vendored into the build's own
#      artifact folder instead of being referenced from an external tree.
# Result, measured on this box with NO PCGen env vars set at all: root-full
# PASSES, 5930 passed across 533 binaries, zero `test result: FAILED` lines.
# All five suites named in the entries below now pass. Counted by awk and
# re-counted by an independent python parse, which agreed exactly:
#   awk '/^test result:/ { for (i=1;i<=NF;i++) if ($(i+1)=="passed;") total+=$i } \
#        END { print total+0 }' root-full.log                    -> 5930
#   awk '/^     Running /{n++} END{print n+0}' root-full.log     ->  533
# The floors were left where they were by the run that wrote this note, since
# raising a floor is a deliberate, separately reviewable act. They have since
# been raised by the 9-of-9 gate run: 5917 -> 5930 and 531 -> 533, each
# reconciled by name in its own entry below.
#
# The hand-counting guidance itself still stands — verify.sh prints MEASURED
# only for stages that passed, so a stage that fails for any OTHER reason
# still has to be counted from its log, and `grep -o` is still unsafe for it:
#
#   grep -oP '^test result: \w+\. \K\d+' root-full.log | paste -sd+ | bc
#
# THAT COMMAND IS NOT SAFE IN EVERY SHELL, and it under-reports silently rather
# than failing. Some agent harnesses shim `grep` to `ugrep`; ugrep 7.5.0's `-o`
# emitted 526 of the 527 matching lines on a real 9279-line root-full.log,
# dropping one `2 passed` and reporting 5823 where the truth is 5825. `grep -c`
# and `grep -n` both matched all 527 on the same file, so nothing looked wrong.
# It reproduced identically on three consecutive runs — this is a quiet wrong
# answer, not a flake.
#
# Count with awk instead. This is byte-for-byte the counter verify.sh itself
# gates on (`sum_passed`, verify.sh:179), so a hand count and the gate can no
# longer disagree:
#
#   awk '/^test result:/ { for (i=1;i<=NF;i++) if ($(i+1)=="passed;") total+=$i } \
#        END { print total+0 }' root-full.log
#   awk '/^     Running /{n++} END{print n+0}' root-full.log
#
# Cross-check with a third implementation before moving a floor. On the
# 2026-07-31 reach-closure sweep, awk, GNU grep 3.11 and a python re-parse all
# returned 5825/526 on BOTH full runs; only the ugrep-shimmed `grep -o`
# dissented. `command grep` bypasses a shell-function shim if you need GNU grep
# specifically.

