# ===========================================================================
# LIVE BASELINES — the only assignments this file makes.
# ===========================================================================
#
# Everything above this line is the dated measurement record, and every value
# in it is now prefixed `#   (historical)`. It used to be live shell.
#
# THE DEFECT THIS CLOSES (SD-29 Epic 10 run 2, 2026-08-13; deferred here from
# run 1). `scripts/verify.sh` SOURCES this file, so every assignment executed
# and the LAST one for a key won. There were 34 assignments for 8 keys:
#
#   $ grep -cE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' scripts/verify-baselines.env   -> 34
#   $ grep -oE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' scripts/verify-baselines.env \
#       | sort -u | wc -l                                               -> 8
#
# Two consequences, both real and neither hypothetical:
#   1. No reader could tell which of ten `BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS=` lines was
#      the gate's actual floor without simulating a shell's last-wins rule.
#   2. A revision written into the middle of the file rather than appended to
#      the end was DEAD ON ARRIVAL and silently so — the gate kept using a
#      later line. Nothing in the file or in verify.sh said appending was
#      load-bearing.
#
# The values below are byte-identical to what sourcing the pre-change file
# produced, verified before and after by:
#   ( set -a; . scripts/verify-baselines.env; set +a; \
#     for k in $(grep -oE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' scripts/verify-baselines.env \
#                | sort -u | tr -d '='); do echo "$k=${!k}"; done )
# No floor was lowered and no ceiling was raised by this change. To move one,
# edit it HERE and record the measurement above, per this file's header.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raised by SD-29 Epic 5 extend round 11 (`sd29-monster-final-r1`,
# `decisions.md §68`) from that round's OWN gate measurement, not from an
# estimate: `./scripts/verify.sh` full run at commit 43ea54a1 reported
# `root-lib (1752 passed)` and
# `root-full (6320 passed across 544 suites, all 525 tests/*.rs suites executed)`.
# The +4 on both is this round's four new `rules_tables::horror_adventures`
# monster tests; `root-full` counts the lib suite, which is why one change moves
# both floors by the same amount.
#   (historical) BASELINE_ROOT_LIB_TESTS=1748
#   (historical) BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS=6316
#
# ROOT_FULL LOWERED 6320 -> 6313 by SD-29 Epic 7 round 9 (`sd29-companion-final-r1`,
# `decisions.md §69.4`). **This is a de-duplication, not a deletion, and the
# distinction is the whole justification** — this file's header says a floor
# that dropped means tests were deleted, "which is the finding, not the fix", so
# the finding is stated here in full and every claim in it is checkable.
#
# `src/bin/gen_book_cache.rs` carried `#[path]` duplicates of
# `rules_tables/advanced_race_guide/mod.rs` and `rules_tables/archetype_swap.rs`
# — a write-scope workaround from an era when `rules_tables/mod.rs` was outside
# the granted surface. A `#[path]`-included module is compiled INTO the binary's
# own crate, so `advanced_race_guide::archetype_tables`'s 7 unit tests were built
# and run TWICE per `cargo test`: once in the lib suite and once again inside the
# `gen_book_cache` bin target. `root-full` counts every target, so the floor had
# been counting those 7 twice since the duplicate was added.
#
# Round 9 retired the duplicates (ARG gained a `companion` family, and a
# `#[path]`-included `mod.rs` resolves `super::` against the BINARY's crate root
# where there is no `companion_chassis`, so `mod companion_data;` compiled in the
# library and failed in the generator). The binary now reaches ARG through the
# library crate, exactly as it already reached `pathfinder_unchained`.
#
# The 7 are named, and they still run — the round's own gate log shows each one
# exactly once, under the lib suite:
#
#   grep -c 'advanced_race_guide::archetype_tables::tests::' root-full.log  -> 7
#     catalog_has_59_records, keys_are_unique_within_book,
#     every_master_record_carries_a_real_description,
#     the_type_and_ability_lists_genuinely_disagree,
#     every_grant_names_a_real_level_and_key,
#     no_internal_category_bookkeeping_grant_is_present,
#     resolved_grant_descriptions_are_the_real_count
#
# BASELINE_ROOT_LIB_TESTS is UNCHANGED at 1752, which is the corroborating
# measurement: if the 7 had been deleted rather than de-duplicated, the lib floor
# would have dropped by the same 7 and it did not. 6320 - 7 = 6313.
#   (historical) BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS=6320   # counted the ARG duplicate twice
#   (historical) BASELINE_ROOT_LIB_TESTS=1752, BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS=6313
